TITLE:: StammerView
summary:: Stammer's display
categories:: Libraries>Stammer
related:: Classes/Stammer, Classes/FxParamView, Classes/FxDevicePanel

DESCRIPTION::
What link::Classes/FxDevicePanel:: puts at the top of Stammer's window: one interval as a strip of steps, a sixteenth each, the beats numbered (more than one interval when the hold runs past its end). Top to bottom:

table::
## strong::steps:: || the run it holds, lit in yellow from the step where it goes, fainter as code::chance:: falls, the chance written on the first step; small flags where it would decide again inside the hold
## strong::in:: || the input as it passed, once sound comes in; the box is the slice it catches, just before it goes; the dashed bar under it, while code::gridVary:: is up, runs from the shortest slice it may take to the longest; the hatching is what code::insert:: mutes while it goes (all of it in code::gate::)
## strong::repeats:: || a block a repeat: as tall as it keeps (code::decay::, code::level::), as low as it falls (code::pitchFall::), the slice drawn backwards in about as many as code::backwards:: says; where the last one ends up written after it; the band, when the filter is on
::

While it runs, a line follows the server's own count (the reply's extras: going or not, which repeat, where the interval is, backwards or not, the slice it took) and the repeat it is really playing lights up in orange.

table::
## strong::in the display:: || strong::does::
## click a step || where it goes (code::offset::)
## drag along the steps || how long (code::hold::)
## the wheel on the steps || the slice (code::grid::)
## double click the steps || back to offset 0, hold 4
## drag the repeats up and down || how far each falls (code::pitchFall::), shift for fine
## the wheel on the repeats || how much each keeps (code::decay::)
## double click the repeats || back to 0 st and 90 %
::

It draws from the object's settings and the replies its meters bring, so it is only live while the window is running; link::Classes/FxParamView:: has the rest.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: unit
The link::Classes/Stammer::.
ARGUMENT:: parent
A view to go in.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: hint
What the hint bar says over it: which lane is under the pointer, its gestures and the values they move.
ARGUMENT:: x
Where the pointer is, across the view.
ARGUMENT:: y
Where the pointer is, down the view.
